{"name":"Demon Blue","hex":"#45538d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"demon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evil supernatural being.\nAn evil being resident in or working for Hell; a devil. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}\n\n A false god or idol; a Satanic divinity. \n A very wicked or malevolent person; also  a mischievous person, especially a child. \nA source (especially personified) of great evil or wickedness; a destructive feeling or character flaw.","An evil being resident in or working for Hell; a devil. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Acronym of distinct electron motion particle: a quasiparticle, a type of massless neutral electron excitation associated with superconductivity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/demon"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Demon","blocks":[{"text":"A demon is an evil or malevolent supernatural entity, though they can be benevolent too. Historically, belief in demons, or stories about demons, occurs in folklore, mythology, religion, occultism, and literature; these beliefs are reflected in media including fiction, comics, film, television, and video games. Belief in demons probably goes back to the Paleolithic age, stemming from humanity's fear of the unknown, the strange and the horrific. In ancient Near Eastern religions and in the Abrahamic religions, including early Judaism and ancient-medieval Christian demonology, a demon is considered a harmful spiritual entity that may cause demonic possession, calling for an exorcism. Large portions of Jewish demonology, a key influence on Christianity and Islam, originated from a later form of Zoroastrianism, and was transferred to Judaism during the Persian era."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/PazuzuDemonAssyria1stMillenniumBCE_no_CGI_dropshadow_-_gradient_based_on.jpg/330px-PazuzuDemonAssyria1stMillenniumBCE_no_CGI_dropshadow_-_gradient_based_on.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demon"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Mephistopheles2.jpg/500px-Mephistopheles2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Mephistopheles2.jpg/1280px-Mephistopheles2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Mephistopheles2.jpg/500px-Mephistopheles2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campai